hus, prolonged periods of\nadditional rainfall over these regions would trigger a similar\nresponse. The current precipitation forecast suggests larger peaks in\nseveral creeks and rivers than what has been observed over the\nprevious 7 days. However, high end probabilistic rainfall amounts\n(i.e. above 90th percentile) may lead to rivers exceeding action\nstage to minor flooding. Most probable basins to see significant\nrises include; the Rio Blanco, San Juan, Piedra, Los Pinos/Vallecito\nCreek, and the Animas River Basins.\n\nConvective storms and periods of heavy rainfall fed from said\ntropical moisture could result in localized flooding impacts across\nthe CWA, however, confidence decreases rapidly north of the San\nJuans. Please continue to monitor the forecast as these systems\nevolve. Especially for those who reside and/or plan to recreate in\nthe southwest quadrant of the forecast area.","ends":"2026-09-30T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Dolores, CO; Gunnison, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Montezuma, CO; Ouray, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ce67801ec73048f07c44dd0418c6a50edd1c8fdc.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ce67801ec73048f07c44dd0418c6a50edd1c8fdc.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-09-29T20:38:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 292038 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 238 PM MDT Tue Sep 29 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Widespread rainfall, heavy at times, remains likely across the far southern portions of our forecast area late tonight through early Thursday. A sharp gradient in QPF still likely across the Denver metro. - Flood Watch in effect for southern Lincoln and fa","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-09-29T18:57:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through 